<title>UK: HSBC up as Hang Seng hits record.</title>
<headline>HSBC up as Hang Seng hits record.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in HSBC Holdings Plc were up around one percent, against a weaker banking sector trend on Friday as Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index closed at a new all-time high, driven mostly by a three-percent surge in HSBC Holdings.</p>
<p>By 1000 GMT, HSBC were up 15-1/2 pence to 18.95 stg.</p>
<p>&quot;This follows the strong lead of Hong Kong's bourse&quot;, one trader said.</p>
<p>The Hang Seng ended 341.21 points or 2.37 percent higher on Friday to a record closing level of 14,757.81. HSBC Holdings closed $HK7.00 higher to $HK235.00, also a record peak.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
